nsit pass\nOpting out\nOpting in\nSummer UPass\nFrequently asked questions\nTerms and conditions\nResearch and Innovation\nResearch and Innovation\nDalhousie is one of Canada's top 15 research-intensive universities. Thought leaders come here to make impactful discoveries that change our world for the better.\nResearch and Innovation overview\nAbout us\nStrategic research direction\nOffice of the Vice-President, Research and Innovation\nOffice of Research Services\nDal Partners\nDal Innovates\nResearch excellence\nAnnual report\nDalSolutions\nStrategic research clusters\nSustainable ocean\nSustainable food systems\nHealthy people, communities, and populations\nClimate tech and clean energy\nCulture and society\nAI and digital innovation\nInnovation and industry partnerships\nEntrepreneurship\nR&D partnerships\nCollaboration\nCentres and institutes\nIndigenous engagement\nSupport for researchers\nInternal funding\nExternal funding\nResponsible conduct of research\nIndigenous research resources\nWomen in research caucus\nCore research facilities\nROMEO researcher portal\nAlumni\nAbout Dal\nAbout Dal\nDalhousie University combines exceptional student experience, high-impact research, and a deep sense of social responsibility in Nova Scotia, Canada.\nAbout Dal overview\nMission, vision, and values\nStrategic plan\nImpact on Global Goals\nEquity, diversity, inclusion and accessibility\nSustainability\nFacts, figures and rankings\nCommunity Hub\nGlobal Relations\nRespectful discourse\nMi'kmaq and Indigenous Relations\nAfrican Nova Scotian connections\nBe Well at Dal\nLeadership and governance\nOur leadership\nGoverning bodies\nAcademic integrity\nUniversity policies\nBudget and finance\nOur story\nTraditions\nHistory\nThe Dal Brand\nCampus locations\nHalifax\nTruro and Bible Hill\nSaint John\nYarmouth\nGetting to campus\nFuture of Campuses\nCape Breton\nContact us\nSocial Media Directory\nHome\nStudy\nExplore Programs\nGraduate & Professional programs\nMaterials Engineering (PhD)\nMaterials Engineering (PhD)\nBenefit from significant industry collaboration.\nProgram Type\nPhD\nFaculties\nEngineering\nGraduate Studies\nUnit\nDepartment of Mechanical Engineering\nLocation\nHalifax\nProgram Start\nSeptember, January, May\nProgram Options\nThesis\nApply now\nExplore the Faculty of Graduate Studies\nWhy choose this program?\nChoose the Materials Engineering (PhD) for its strong research record, industry collaboration, and diverse study fields from materials production to advanced processing. Benefit from cutting-edge research opportunities, practical industry applications, and the potential for significant publishable work.\nCareers\nAdvance your career in aerospace, automotive, electronics, energy, biomedical, materials production and recycling, corrosion and wear resistance, electronic materials development, or composite materials design. Possible careers include:\nPossible careers include:\nMaterials engineer\nProcess engineer\nQuality assurance specialist\nResearch scientist\nAdmission requirements\nYou'll need to meet the Faculty of Graduate Studies minimum requirements as well as any program-specific admission requirements before you can apply.\nProgram-specific admission requirements\nLearn more about the admissions requirements for international students.\nFinancial information\nAt Dalhousie, we want our students to focus on their studies, rather than worry about their personal finances.\nLearn more about tuition, fees, and scholarships\nProgram options\nThesis: Pursue independent and original research guided by a supervisor to develop and defend your thesis.\nStandard program duration:\n5 years or longer\nEnrolment options:\nFull-time\nDelivery format:\nIn-person\nExplore program options\nAll graduate programs at Dalhousie are collaboratively delivered by a home Faculty and the Faculty of Graduate Studies.\nContact an admissions advisor\nGRADUATE COORDINATOR\nRobert Bauer\nEmail: Robert.bauer@dal.ca\nPhone: 902-494-1288\nI'm ready to apply!\nStart my application\nLearn more about Dalhousie's application process\nQuestions about graduate studies at Dal?\nConnect with a member of the Faculty of Graduate Studies\nWhile every effort is made to ensure accuracy on this page, in the event of a discrepancy, Dalhousie's Academic Calendars are the official reference.\nVisit\nMaps and parking\nCampus tours\nCampus locations\nLibraries\nConnect\nCampus directory\nMedia Centre\nContact us\nFollow Dal on social\nExplore\nCareers\nUpcoming events\nCommunity Hub\nDalNews\nDalhousie University operates in the unceded territories of the Mi\u2019kmaw, Wolastoqey, and Peskotomuhkati Peoples. These sovereign nations hold inherent rights as the original peoples of these lands, and we each carry collective obligations under the Peace and Friendship Treaties. Section 35 of the Constitution Act, 1982 recognizes and affirms Aboriginal and Treaty rights in Canada.\nView the full land acknowledgement statement\nWe recognize that African Nova Scotians are a distinct people whose histories, legacies and contributions have enriched that part of Mi'kma'ki known as Nova Scotia for over 400 years.\nView our African Nova Scotian acknowledgement\n\u00a9 Dalhousie University\nAccessibility\nWebsite feedback\nPrivacy Statement\nTerms of Use", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://www.dal.ca/study/programs/graduate-professional/materials-engineering-phd.html#main_content"], ["Donate", "https://www.givecampus.com/campaigns/74605/donations/new"], ["Libraries", "https://libraries.dal.ca/"], ["Campus Maps", "https://www.dal.ca/campusmaps"], ["Campus Tours", "https://www.dal.ca/admissions/campus-tours.html"], ["People Directory", "https://directory.dal.ca/"], ["Events", "https://events.dal.ca/"], ["New Students", "https://www.dal.ca/information-new-students.html"], ["Current Students", "https://www.dal.ca/life-at-dal.html"], ["Faculty and Staff", "https://www.dal.ca/information-faculty-staff.html"], ["Alumni", "https://www.dal